"Before The Wooden Gates"
"Rising up before you to the south are a pair of large wooden gates.  Etched
into each of the gates is the image of a delicate white rose on a blood-red
shield.  Spanning out around you to the northeast and northwest are vast
rolling hills that extend for miles.  To the north the worn, wagon-rutted
Southern Trade Road journeys off over the rolling hills of the wilds.
"
