#89002
"Intersection of Brembledon and Shorly Avenue"
"Spanning out before you to the south, southwest, and southeast is the lush,
hilly village of Brembledon.  Large and small houses covered in grass dot the
verdant landscape of the town.  The roads are covered in deep wagon ruts which
cut through the low grass.  The land rises and falls due to the builders
taking no time to flatten the landscape, leaving it as is.  The signs point to
Brembledon Avenue lying to the east and west, circling the borders of the
town.  The signs also point to Shorly Avenue continuing north and further
southward.
"
