shrubs are young trees with several leafless branches.  The grass here has
been slowly torn away from the dirt from the many feet which constantly tread
across it on a daily basis, leaving large patches of dirt which have turned
into mud puddles scattered about the lane.  To the east and west, Brembledon
Avenue continues its course through the village.
