wall that stretches high enough to prevent even taller creatures from
trespassing.  Spaced a few yards apart atop the wall are a few banners that
flap vigorously in the air.  Growing at the base of the wall are several
bushes shaped in the figure of a pony, rabbit, and dog.  Looking north, the
avenue passes by a row of small houses.  To the west, Egerdon Street continues
its journey around the town, becoming slightly more level with the grass
seeming to grow slightly taller in that direction.
