#89040
"Corner of Brembledon Avenue and Egerdon Street"
"Sunndydale Lane and Egerdon Street intersect with each other at this point. 
In the center of the road is a towering oak tree which stands at least thirty
feet high.  It rich, dark brown bark is mottled with bits of green moss.  At
the base of the tree, someone has taken the time to plant small yellow lilacs
and pink daisies.  Wagon ruts run around each side of the tree, heading off in
every direction.  Directly to the east the massive eastern gates of the city
rise up.  Brembledon Avenue heads west as it makes its way back into the
center of the city.  Egerdon Street continues its north-south course from this
point.
"
