west sides are small stalls each containing a different size and type of mount
ranging from small packmules to muscular warhorses.  Set in front of each
stall are water troughs and barrels of grain.  Hanging from the wall next to
the door to the north are several saddles, bridles, combs and grooming
supplies for the animals.  An open doorway to the north leads to the back of
the building where the steady clanging of metal can be heard.
"
