wall of this building.  Forging hammers and metal tongs hang from the western
wall and beneath them resting on a wooden shelf are several stacks of horse
shoes.  The eastern side of the room is cluttered with stacks of saddles,
bridles, and various types of barding.  In the center of the room is a
life-sized dummy of a heavy warhorse on which rests a suit of highly-polished
scale mail barding.  To the south an opening in the wall leads into another
section of the building.
"
